# The Session data

## Notation fixes

This fork fixes small notation errors in the ABC data. The [current issue list](reports/status.md) separates applied fixes, unresolved findings, pickup and ending cases, and syntax the checker does not handle. See [CHANGES.md](CHANGES.md) for the changes and [changes/](changes/) for the complete ABC before and after each fix.

The source is [adactio/TheSession-data at 9106aa8](https://github.com/adactio/TheSession-data/tree/9106aa8e29b72c3affd954f48b259ea02a1fb418). Original contributors, IDs and metadata are retained. The database continues under ODbL 1.0, with the full upstream content terms preserved in [LICENSE.md](LICENSE.md).

CSV, JSON and SQLite contain the same fixes. To check them, materialize Git LFS files and run `python3 tools/apply.py`. Run `python3 tools/apply.py --apply` to reapply the recorded changes to their exact source text. An unexpected source edit stops the operation.

To find and verify further typos using a local TradMate checkout and its pinned Dart parser:

```bash
python3 tools/fix_notation.py --tradmate-repo /path/to/TradMate --dart /path/to/dart --apply
```

The command checks repeated phrases, compares playback events, rescans until no further supported changes remain, updates all exports and rebuilds the issue lists. It does not push Git changes. Omitting `--apply` writes proposals and checks to `reports/` without changing the data. See [the tool notes](tools/README.md) for details and requirements.

## Database and export checks

The [full integrity report](reports/database-integrity/README.md) compares every table with its CSV and JSON exports and checks references, setting identities, set copies and map locations. SQLite now includes unique `tune_ids` and `setting_ids` parent tables, with corresponding exports. Original source-table metadata and row IDs are retained. Recording entries can retain empty optional tune references. See the report for the schema repair and unresolved set-position observations.

```bash
python3 tools/database_relations.py
python3 tools/audit_database.py
```

The [further parser review](reports/further-parser-review/README.md) adds an independent abc2svg check of the remaining notation findings.

## Upstream project information

CSV and JSON files of data from [The Session](https://thesession.org/):

* [tunes](https://thesession.org/tunes/),
* [sessions](https://thesession.org/sessions/),
* [events](https://thesession.org/events/),
* [recordings](https://thesession.org/recordings/),
* [sets of tunes](https://thesession.org/tunes/sets),
* aliases of tune names,
* popularity of tunes.

I'll try to update the files once a week.

If anyone wants to convert the data to other formats, feel free to fork the project and send me a pull request.

If this data is useful to you, please [donate money to the upkeep of The Session](https://thesession.org/donate).
